>I was successful to compile gcc-2.5.2 on my DEC 3000/400. I did not
>try later versions. But I did NOT succeed in compiling libg++. Any
>experience on this? Has somebody successfully compiled libg++? Does it
>work on a DEC-Alpha?

There are a couple of known problems with g++ on the alpha.  the most notable
of which is that calling virtual functions in multiply inherited classes
is broken.  As a result the compiling of libg++ has been disabled.  Editing the
config.in file should allow you to re-enable compiling on the alpha.  Editing,
cp-call.c around line 420

/* FIXME: This is what breaks vtables on the alpha.  */
*ptr_to_instptr = build (PLUS_EXPR, TREE_TYPE (*ptr_to_instptr),
				*ptr_to_instptr,
				convert (integer_type_node, build_component_ref .......
                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
so that the integer_type_node becomes ptr_type_node should solve the above
problem with g++.

It would recomend using 2.5.4 as it includes another Alpha specific patch.

There are still a couple of know problems, but as long as you don't try to
optimize and don't use alot of sign extension things should be serviceable.


