Hi,
  [I looked in the OSF/Ultrix FAQ, and didn't find anything there]

  We've just gotten our first OSF/1 beastie so I'm new at this.

  On an X-Windows terminal you normally have a chooser displaying
  a list of hosts.  Once you select a host, you get a login box
  from that host.  Now, if you don't have a valid login on the
  host you chose, you need to somehow abort the login box and drop
  back to the chooser.  In mit X11R5, I use:
	...
	xlogin*login.translations: #override\
		Ctrl<Key>R: abort-display()\n\
	...
  in /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xresources.  Then, a Ctrl-R will abort
  your login box and drop you back to the chooser.  (Ctrl-C also
  works, dunno why).

  This method **doesn't** work when I get a login box from the Dec
  OSF/1 computer.  No matter what I try there is no way that I can
  determine, short of rebooting the X-windows terminal, to abort from
  the login box.  There's even that nice "abort" button in the bottom
  right corner of the login box window.  It doesn't work either.

  In /usr/lib/X11/xdm, in Xresources, I've tried changing:
	dxlogin*GpiLoginPrompt.NameField.translations: #override\n\
  However, it ignores:
  		:Ctrl<Key>R: abort-display()\n\
  and 		:Ctrl<Key>C: abort-session()\n\ 
  and even 	:Ctrl<Key>C: abort-login()\n\

  For that matter, it also ignores the "<F1> key instead of return 
  starts a failsafe session" resource,
		:<Key>F1: activate() next-tab-group()\n\
  and that resource was configured that way by the vendor -- it's
  even documented in the man page!!

Can any Dec OSF/1 X11 gurus shed some light on this?
Thanks much!  Email is preferred.
...art

