      Nine Digital Vice Presidents To Attend DECUS '93/San Francisco

         Several VPs and Senior Managers Will Also Participate In
                     Special Digital Listens! Session


SHREWSBURY, Mass., November 22, 1993 -- Nine Digital Equipment Corporation 
vice presidents will participate in DECUS '93/San Francisco.  Several of 
these vice presidents, along with Digital senior managers, will participate 
in a special Digital Listens! session at the national event, which is 
sponsored by the U.S. Chapter of the Digital Equipment Computer Users 
Society (DECUS).

Edward Lucente, vice president, Worldwide Sales and Marketing, will deliver 
the keynote address at DECUS '93/San Francisco on Monday, December 6 at 
8:00 a.m. in room 103/104 of the Moscone Convention Center in San 
Francisco, Calif.  Entitled, "The Open Client/Server Advantage," Lucente 
will describe his vision for open client/server computing and the 
challenges faced by companies trying to tie their people, business and 
technology objectives together for competitive advantage.  

Eight additional executives will participate in the weeklong national 
event, which runs from December 4 - 10.  The national event also features 
in-depth seminars, technical symposium sessions, a multivendor trade show 
and a Digital Technology Center. The seminars and sessions run December 4 - 
10 and the trade show runs December 7 - 9.

Key executives taking part in DECUS '93/San Francisco include:  Jesse 
Lipcon, vice president, Windows NT; William Demmer, vice president, 
Computer Systems Group; Charles Christ, vice president, Storage Business 
Unit; Peter Mercury, vice president, Operations, Multivendor Technology 
Support; Rose Ann Giordano, vice president, Production Systems Software and 
Corporate Officer for DECUS; Robert Schmitt, vice president, U.S. 
Marketing; Robert Jolls, vice president, Product and Services Marketing; 
and Bud Enright, vice president, Product Marketing.

On Monday, December 6, William Demmer will present an Alpha AXP Hardware 
and Software Update at 9:00 a.m. in Room 103/104.  Also on Monday, Charles 
Christ will take part in a session on Digital Storage Systems Announcements 
at 1:00 p.m. in Room 103/104.

Peter Mercury will speak about Multivendor Technology Support on Tuesday, 
December 7, at 10:00 a.m. in Room 310.  He will also discuss Digital 
Services Solutions in the afternoon at 1:00 p.m. in Room 202/210.

Jesse Lipcon will deliver the keynote address for a special spotlight on 
Windows NT program, which will be held from December 8 - 10.  In his 
address on Wednesday, December 8, at 9:00 a.m. in Room 103/104, Lipcon will 
speak about Windows NT and the future of Digital.

Digital Listens! Session

On Tuesday, December 7, Rose Ann Giordano and Robert Schmitt will be joined 
by other Digital vice presidents and senior managers in a special Digital 
Listens! session at 11:00 a.m. in Room 202/210.  Open to all attendees, the 
forum will encourage user feedback on issues relating to their relationship 
with Digital.

DECUS '93/San Francisco is a one-week event featuring in-depth seminars, 
technical symposium sessions, a multivendor trade show and the Digital 
Technology Center.  The sessions and seminars run December 4 - 10 and the 
trade show runs December 7 - 9.  Two new additions this year are an 
in-depth Spotlight on Windows NT and technology streams on PATHWORKS 5.0 
migration, Internet usage and electronic mail.

DECUS members solve their organizations' computing problems and stay 
informed about industry issues and emerging technologies with the aid of 
the U.S. Chapter's semiannual national seminars, symposium and trade show 
event; regional conferences; Special Interest and Local Users Groups; 
electronic conferencing system; and public domain library.  

