 DECUS '93/SAN FRANCISCO PROVIDES BRIDGE TO SUCCESS IN MULTIPLATFORM WORLD

          DECUS National Event To Unveil Spotlight On Windows NT
                       And New Special Topic Streams



Building on its successful national event this past June in Atlanta, DECUS 
'93/San Francisco will feature some of the most comprehensive, 
multiplatform programs available today in the computer industry.  The 
semi-annual national event is sponsored by the U.S. Chapter of the Digital 
Equipment Computer Users Society (DECUS).

Two new additions to the event are an in-depth spotlight on Windows NT and 
technology streams on migrating to PATHWORKS 5.0, effective use of the 
Internet, and solving the electronic mail puzzle.

DECUS '93/San Francisco will be held from Saturday, December 4, 1993 
through Friday, December 10, 1993 at the Moscone Convention Center.  The 
national event provides the most comprehensive computer industry experience 
with over 100 seminars, 1,100 symposium sessions, 125+ multiplatform 
computing vendors and the most comprehensive educational display of Digital 
Equipment Corporation technology.  

A special Windows NT program, "Integrating Windows NT Into Your 
Multiplatform Environment," will include 35 sessions December 8 - 9, and 
five all-day seminars on December 10.  This program, along with streams of 
topics, seminars, symposium sessions and the DECUS trade show, will provide 
participants with valuable knowledge on how to successfully move into a 
multiplatform environment.

Additionally, Edward Lucente, vice president of Worldwide Sales and 
Marketing at Digital Equipment Corporation, will deliver a keynote address 
entitled, "The Open Client/Server Advantage," on Monday, December 6, at 
8:00 a.m.   

Seminars and Symposium Sessions 

The DECUS Seminars program will be held Saturday and Sunday, and will 
feature over 100 one- and two-day, in-depth training seminars.  Each 
seminar will focus on a specific technical topic, including network 
integration, system tuning, Alpha AXP, OpenVMS, TCP/IP, database 
management, disaster recovery, Microsoft Windows, ULTRIX, UNIX and OSF/1.

DECUS symposium sessions, which run from Monday through Friday, feature 
over 1,100 tutorials, clinics and workshops covering technical issues, 
management issues, applications, platforms and technologies.  The symposium 
sessions will cover topics such as system and network management, office 
automation, personal computing, security, artificial intelligence, storage 
systems, operating systems, business practices, languages, process 
engineering, programming and database engines, among others.


DECUS Trade Show And Digital Technology Center

Following its successful debut at DECUS '93/Atlanta, the DECUS Trade Show 
is now a regular part of the DECUS national event.  The show will feature 
over 125 multiplatform computing vendors, including WordPerfect, Ross 
Systems, Information Builders, Executive Software, Oracle Corporation, and 
The ASK Group. The Trade Show will showcase the newest leading edge 
products, services and technologies for multiplatform environments.  It 
will open on Tuesday and run through Thursday.

The DECUS national event also features the largest regular showing of 
Digital and Digital-related partners' products, services and technologies.  
The Digital Technology Center gives attendees the opportunity to view and 
test products while meeting with developers, product managers and other 
experienced users. 

Participants who register by the early-bird deadline, November 15, will 
receive a discount on registration fees.  To register early call 
1-800-DECUS55.

DECUS members solve their organizations' computing problems and stay 
informed about industry issues and emerging technologies with the aid of 
the Chapter's semiannual national seminars, symposium and trade show event; 
regional conferences; local seminars program; Special Interest and Local 
Users Groups; electronic conferencing system; and public domain library.  

