The question can be read two ways because it does not state whether he
wants to perform the function from user space or from kernel space.

My original answer is correct if he is writing a user space application
that needs to lock its pages into physical memory (which is what I
thought he was asking).  This can be coded without access to the
source, just like any other libc function.

If he is writing kernel code, he should use the vm_map_pageable()
function, which is documented in the device driver reference.
Assuming the proper competence, the device driver reference should
contain enough information so that the function can be called 
without having access to the kernel's source code.

