> kernel (Process 0) has 292 M. But swap seems to be normal.

In OSF 1.2 (I haven't got 1.3 yet) we had problems of memory leaks in the X
server (I vaguely remember reporting them to DEC). My fix to this was to force
the X server to reboot every time someone logs out. This can be done by adding
changing /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers to something like

:0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -once

Also adding to the xdm-config file:

DisplayManager._0.terminateServer:    true

I'm not sure which one of these did the trick (maybe both are needed), but I
can remember the suggested method of doing this (listed on this group before)
failed to work for me.

Hope this helps,

	James


