: The memory usage always grows and NEVER shrinks.

I have the same problem with our mailserver (a DEC 3000/400 running OSF/1
1.3, lazy swap).  Swapon -s reports increasingly large amounts of reserved
space use over time until I eventually need to reboot.  I'm still trying to
isolate the factors that may be causing it.

: Especially the X-Server had a size of 135 M after some days. After
: rebooting, X now has 11 M with the first user logged on. Now the
: kernel (Process 0) has 292 M. But swap seems to be normal.

Just add a -terminate on your X server entry in /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers,
like:

:0	local	/usr/bin/X11/X -bs -su -terminate

Then restart your xdm process with

	/sbin/init.d/xdm restart

