I think it would be fair to point out that OSF is the only major OS to
allow one to change the swapping strategy.  In this way
"mission-critical" machines can guarantee that they won't crash from
running out of swap and the rest of us don't need that much swap at all.

It is possibly a mistake that factory installed machines come with
'eager' swap allocation.  It generates a lot of confusion until one gets
round to reading the Sys Admin manual.

In fact swap usage seems to have decreased in general under 1.3 compared
to 1.2.


