In article <CAN.93Nov5174759@shrimp.cam-orl.co.uk>, can@cam-orl.co.uk (Cosmos Nicolaou) writes:
|> does anyone know how to configure their osf1.2 kernel to use more mbufs
|> than the default?

Edit the /sys/conf/HOSTNAME file, change mbclusters to the desired
value, cd /sys/conf && doconfig -c HOSTNAME && cp /sys/HOSTNAME/vmunix /
and reboot (more or less...).

Of course, you should read the DEC Sysadmin manual for all the
details - I'm just giving the short answers and am making no
guarantee that you won't shoot yourself in the foot by doing
this...

